{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340842",
      "title": "Caching Differences: Development vs Production",
      "lectureOrder": 180,
      "videoOrder": 166,
      "sourceHash": "ca6cb378b6fe5d4561afbba2e815979d45de2cb7f7e12f83958b761464921f99",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 1.53,
          "en": "Now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.53,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "we're almost done with this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "As you see, we can now update the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 8.73,
          "en": "we can add new posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.73,
          "end": 12.72,
          "en": "This all works, but here's something that won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 16.683,
          "en": "Let's say we're done and we wanna deploy this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.79,
          "end": 19.8,
          "en": "What we would do then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 23.25,
          "en": "is that we would build the application for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.25,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "We would trigger a process that's provided by NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 29.97,
          "en": "that prepares the application for deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.97,
          "end": 32.94,
          "en": "and that performs the various optimizations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 35.04,
          "en": "and preparation steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.04,
          "end": 38.07,
          "en": "To start that process you can simply run a script",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.07,
          "end": 42.123,
          "en": "that's part of the NextJS project by running npm run build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 45,
          "en": "That's what you would typically always do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "before deploying the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 52.65,
          "en": "Now this will then go through that build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.65,
          "end": 57.09,
          "en": "and once it's done, it will give you a folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.09,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "next folder, which you can deploy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 62.07,
          "en": "For now I don't wanna deploy it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.07,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "Instead, what I wanna do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "is I wanna preview that deployable application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 70.53,
          "en": "So now I wanna run this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.53,
          "end": 73.8,
          "en": "not in development mode, but in production mode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.8,
          "end": 77.19,
          "en": "still on my computer here to test it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.19,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "but without all those extra development mode features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 83.13,
          "en": "And we can do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.13,
          "end": 87.57,
          "en": "after running npm run build by running npm start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.57,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "That will start a production Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.39,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "of this NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "Now this Server will still be available on local host 3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 100.02000000000001,
          "en": "and therefore I can simply reload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.02000000000001,
          "end": 103.8,
          "en": "but it will now be the production version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.8,
          "end": 106.25999999999999,
          "en": "And one thing you can immediately see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.25999999999999,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "is that as I switch those pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "that loading text doesn't appear here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "Instead the data is there instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "Great. It's faster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 118.32,
          "en": "Yeah, but this comes with a price",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.32,
          "end": 121.893,
          "en": "and you can see that price if I create a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "Let's say I wanna share a post about a great vacation I had,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "I prepare the image for that, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 133.26,
          "en": "and I click create post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.26,
          "end": 135.12,
          "en": "That's all looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.12,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "I'm redirected to the feed page and where's my post?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 139.74,
          "en": "It's not there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.74,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "And it's also not there if I reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "It's also not on the starting page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 147.15,
          "en": "And that is something we did not encounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.15,
          "end": 148.14,
          "en": "during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.14,
          "end": 151.77,
          "en": "but we do encounter now in production mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.77,
          "end": 153.42000000000002,
          "en": "Because I did mention before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 157.47,
          "en": "that NextJS performs some pretty aggressive caching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.47,
          "end": 161.04,
          "en": "And again, I'll get back to that in the next section again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 163.35,
          "en": "But what NextJS does in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.35,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "when preparing this page for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 171.89,
          "en": "is it pre renders all your pages during that build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.02,
          "end": 175.29,
          "en": "and caches those pre-rendered pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 179.55,
          "en": "And it's then never re-renders them thereafter then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.55,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "unless there are dynamic pages with dynamic segments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 184.743,
          "en": "which we don't have here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.73,
          "end": 189.66,
          "en": "So these pages were pre-rendered and they stay that way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.66,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "So any changes to the data aren't picked up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 194.03,
          "en": "And that's of course not great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.12,
          "end": 196.98,
          "en": "Now what can we do about that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.98,
          "end": 199.47,
          "en": "Well, we have to tell NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.47,
          "end": 202.53,
          "en": "that it should re-render some of these pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 205.44,
          "en": "whenever we change the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "And we can do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 209.433,
          "en": "with help of the revalidatePath function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.27,
          "end": 214.53,
          "en": "We are already using that for changing the likes status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.53,
          "end": 218.64,
          "en": "And for that reason, for example, liking does work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 220.92000000000002,
          "en": "and those changes are picked up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.92000000000002,
          "end": 223.44,
          "en": "And you see that now after I liked this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.44,
          "end": 225.69299999999998,
          "en": "suddenly my new post also appeared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 230.61,
          "en": "because when I liked this, I called revalidatePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.61,
          "end": 233.31,
          "en": "and that revalidates all those pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.31,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "and tells NextJS to throw them out of the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 238.98,
          "en": "and recreate them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.98,
          "end": 241.65,
          "en": "But of course, the idea is not that I have to like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.65,
          "end": 245.67,
          "en": "or unlike a post in order to get any new posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.67,
          "end": 247.38,
          "en": "Instead, what we should do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 247.38,
          "end": 250.2,
          "en": "is we should also revalidate the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 250.2,
          "end": 255.2,
          "en": "here inside of our createPost Server Action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.65,
          "end": 260.943,
          "en": "Before I redirect, I wanna call revalidatePath,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.05,
          "end": 266.28,
          "en": "and I wanna make sure that all my pages are revalidated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 266.28,
          "end": 268.323,
          "en": "and get their latest data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 271.8,
          "en": "Now, revalidating all pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "is actually not necessary here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 276.75,
          "en": "because the new post page, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.75,
          "end": 280.65,
          "en": "does not need to be revalidated and recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.65,
          "end": 283.53,
          "en": "But we'll dive deeper into caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 283.53,
          "end": 286.35,
          "en": "and how you can control in greater detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.35,
          "end": 290.13,
          "en": "which parts of the cached data will be revalidated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.13,
          "end": 291.12,
          "en": "in the next section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.12,
          "end": 293.37,
          "en": "For now, I'll just do it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 293.37,
          "end": 296.13,
          "en": "And therefore with that change made,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.13,
          "end": 298.35,
          "en": "if we stop that production server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.35,
          "end": 300.72,
          "en": "and we rebuild the project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.72,
          "end": 302.973,
          "en": "so that the latest code is picked up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.45,
          "end": 310.413,
          "en": "and we then thereafter start that production server again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 311.88,
          "end": 315.85,
          "en": "If I now reload this and create another new post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 316.74,
          "end": 321.74,
          "en": "and I share my experience with the delicious paella I had,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.29,
          "end": 327.99,
          "en": "you'll see that now I'm redirected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 327.99,
          "end": 330.48,
          "en": "after this was uploaded and created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.48,
          "end": 333.03,
          "en": "and I now see that data right from the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 335.28,
          "en": "And I don't have to like or unlike something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 335.28,
          "end": 336.65999999999997,
          "en": "for it to appear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 336.65999999999997,
          "end": 339.75,
          "en": "because now we are revalidating our pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.75,
          "end": 344.55,
          "en": "and our paths there whenever we create a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 344.55,
          "end": 346.77,
          "en": "By the way, on the starting page I only see two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.77,
          "end": 348.48,
          "en": "because there I have some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.48,
          "end": 351.51,
          "en": "to only fetch the latest two posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.51,
          "end": 352.74,
          "en": "So that's not a bug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 352.74,
          "end": 354.933,
          "en": "but instead working the way it should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 355.89,
          "end": 358.59000000000003,
          "en": "And with that, we now finished this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 358.59000000000003,
          "end": 362.91,
          "en": "and you learned a lot about data mutations in NextJS apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.91,
          "end": 366.03,
          "en": "and how to perform them with Server Actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 366.03,
          "end": 369.45,
          "en": "and with a couple of utility hooks and extra features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 369.45,
          "end": 371.463,
          "en": "you also might need quite a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
